WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.490
Donald Trump did end up having a press briefing
yesterday after not having them over the weekend

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:10.690
after the bleach injection fiasco led to him
just walking out without taking questions

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.830
from the Friday press briefing.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:14.849
And it was a really weird one yesterday.

00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:19.480
First that was scheduled as normal for 5 p.m.
as a White House Corona Virus Task Force press

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:20.480
briefing.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.780
Then it was canceled.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:27.600
Then very haphazardly, a Rose Garden press
conference was scheduled to replace the press

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.790
briefing.

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.710
And to Trump's credit, he didn't take questions.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:38.010
But for whatever reason, there was one question
that was even remotely connected to the bleach

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.430
injection fiasco.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:45.100
I've been asking around whether reporters
were warned off of asking questions about

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.150
the bleach fiasco or what.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:53.280
But in any case, the one question that was
asked was about the number of disinfectant

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:58.650
ingestion related phone calls to poison control
centers across the country, which have increased.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:01.850
Does Trump take any responsibility, was the
question.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:02.969
Big shocker.

00:01:02.969 --> 00:01:05.149
He does not take any responsibility.

00:01:05.149 --> 00:01:06.149
Take a look at the video.

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:11.880
Larry Hogan specifically said they've seen
a spike in people using disinfectant after

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.029
your comments last week.

00:01:14.029 --> 00:01:15.229
I know you said they were saké.

00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:16.609
I can't imagine why.

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:17.889
I can't imagine why.

00:01:17.889 --> 00:01:18.889
Yeah.

00:01:18.889 --> 00:01:19.889
Take any responsibility.

00:01:19.889 --> 00:01:20.889
Oh, no, I can't imagine.

00:01:20.889 --> 00:01:22.090
I can't imagine that.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:23.259
Yeah, go ahead, please.

00:01:23.259 --> 00:01:25.020
President, he can't imagine why.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:30.700
Well, because he wondered aloud, what if we
hit the body with an injected disinfectant

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.919
just four days ago?

00:01:31.919 --> 00:01:34.649
That's why the question is being posed to
him.

00:01:34.649 --> 00:01:37.499
And we're now learning of many more instances
of this.

00:01:37.499 --> 00:01:42.740
The reporter there mentioned, Marilyn, the
increase in Maryland of calls to poison control

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.909
related to the ingestion of household cleaners.

00:01:45.909 --> 00:01:48.039
We also have some news out of Kansas.

00:01:48.039 --> 00:01:55.239
In Kansas, a state health officer, Lee Norman,
said poison control saw a 40 percent increase

00:01:55.239 --> 00:02:01.459
in cleaning chemical related cases in the
last few days, including one guy who drank

00:02:01.459 --> 00:02:04.289
a product because someone suggested it.

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:08.789
We don't know whether that someone was Donald
Trump, someone who heard it from Donald Trump

00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:13.180
or just a mere coincidence and not related
to Donald Trump at all.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.709
So here's what I want to ask you about.

00:02:15.709 --> 00:02:21.819
I've been reading the new defense online from
mostly people on the right, but even from

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:24.390
some people on the left kind of agreeing here.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:29.980
And they've been saying, if you are so dumb
that you drink bleach because the president

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:35.860
mentions it as a possible corona virus treatment,
you don't deserve to survive.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:40.370
In other words, it's a sort of Darwinian thinning,
thinning of the herd type of thing, even though

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:46.620
it's obviously not really Darwinian, but it's
colloquially named that if you were this dumb,

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:52.969
that simply because Trump talks about drinking
bleach, you do it, that it is a calling of

00:02:52.969 --> 00:02:57.560
the week, thinning of the herd sort of thing,
and that we shouldn't really worry about it.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:02.950
And it reminds me of this idea that if you
want to thin the herd, you get rid of the

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:06.129
warning labels and just let it happen.

00:03:06.129 --> 00:03:07.129
So what

00:03:07.129 --> 00:03:08.129
do you think?

00:03:08.129 --> 00:03:15.040
I mean, my my reaction tends to be I don't
condemn the cond I condemn the con men.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.560
So it feels weird to me.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.569
Just write it, writing it off that way.

00:03:18.569 --> 00:03:23.459
It's not you know, that it's not the job of
the president.

00:03:23.459 --> 00:03:29.420
It's not excusable that a president says things
that goad dumb people, if that's what you

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:32.280
believe they are into killing themselves.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:38.519
There's a very sort of utilitarian reaction,
which is that a lot of the people aren't dying.

00:03:38.519 --> 00:03:43.549
They're just getting sick enough from drinking
bleach that they need to go into the hospital.

00:03:43.549 --> 00:03:45.200
They require medical services.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.150
They consume medical resources.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:50.780
And it's taking hospital space away from people
who actually just have coronavirus.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:54.000
That would be a very utilitarian reaction.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.659
But a lot of people tweeting me and this seems
to be the predominant reaction, the contempt

00:03:59.659 --> 00:04:03.010
must be for the con men, not for the cond.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:08.379
Ignoring the plight of those who are cond
is not particularly progressive.

00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:09.379
And I agree with that.

00:04:09.379 --> 00:04:10.650
I want to hear from you.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:16.459
Bigger picture, regardless of the cond we
can objectively say a president shouldn't

00:04:16.459 --> 00:04:20.389
be floating such ideas, period, regardless
of the impact that they have.

00:04:20.389 --> 00:04:25.740
One other reaction has been, if you only harm
yourself, then we should be less concerned.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:29.870
It's not even clear to me that people who
fall for this stuff are only harming themselves.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:31.750
They may be suggesting other people do it.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:36.390
They may be harming themselves in a way that
then can leave their children without a parent.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:40.580
The idea of only harming yourself is one that
we would have to grapple with a little more

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.060
more distinctly.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:49.030
Overall, though, people hope to be able to
trust the office of the presidency.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:55.889
Until now, many people have been told you
can trust the office of the presidency.

00:04:55.889 --> 00:04:58.960
So maybe the problem isn't with.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:06.599
The people, but with a system that has allowed
trust in the office of the presidency to be

00:05:06.599 --> 00:05:13.660
so exploited by a con man like Donald Trump,
blaming the frightened masses, so to speak,

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:18.720
as one person said to me on Twitter, rather
than those with the institutional power doesn't

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.000
strike me as progressive.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.030
And I agree with that.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:21.889
But I want to hear from you

